  "description": "EVOPEN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H108 Co4 N2 O30 Tb3 1+,C22 H44 O10 Tb1 1-,2(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.104-3.900 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.14-111.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H164Co4N2O44Tb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
